# Lesson 2, from the point-count exercise hand 7.
title: A strong two-bid
id: L02-11
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.2, 2.5
student: S
board: 11
dealer: S
vulnerable: none

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  9643   952    J82    Q96
  E  KJT85  3      T9     KT732
  S  -      AQJT84 AKQ43  A4
  W  AQ72   K76    765    J85

auction:
  S 2H*    = 22+ points, five or more hearts: forcing
     key: 20 HCP, plus 3 for the void and 1 for the doubleton: 24, with six hearts. Open 2♥. Partner must respond.
     not 1H: With 24 points, a one-bid might be passed out. Did you remember the two-bid?
     not 2D: With six hearts and five diamonds, which suit is longer?
     not 1D: With 24 points, a one-bid might be passed out. Did you remember the two-bid?
     not 2NT: 2NT shows a balanced hand. Is a void balanced?
     not *: With 22+ points and a long suit, which opening makes partner bid?
  W Pass
  N 3H     = Heart support and a few points
  E Pass
  S 4H*    = Game
     key: Partner's raise shows three or more hearts and a smattering of points. With 24 of your own, bid game.
     not Pass: Your 24 points plus partner's raise: is there enough for game?
     not 6H: We won't worry about slams yet, and partner showed very little. 4♥ is enough.
     not *: Your 24 points plus partner's raise: is there enough for game?
  W Pass
  N Pass
  E Pass

auction recap:
  2♥ showed 22+ points and five or more hearts, and partner had to bid.
  Her 3♥ raise said three or more hearts and a smattering of high cards.
  That is plenty for game, so you bid 4♥. You are declarer, because you
  bid hearts first, and so West will lead to the first trick.

planning:
  trumps out: 4
  remind: What is the contract? How many tricks do you need?

play:
  1   W H6  N H2  E H3  S H8
  2   S D3  W D5  N DJ  E D9
      note: The plan: run your diamonds, then trump your black-suit losers. First, cross to dummy's ♦J.
  3   N H5  E C2  S HA  W H7
      note: Lead a trump from dummy to your ♥A.
  4   S DA  W D6  N D2  E DT
      note: Now run your diamonds.
  5   S DK  W D7  N D8  E S5
      note: Keep going.
  6   S DQ  W S2  N C6  E C3
      note: And again.
  7   S D4  W C5  N C9  E C7
      note: Your last diamond is a winner.
  8   S CA  W C8  N CQ  E CT
      note: Cash the ♣A.
  9   S C4  W CJ  N H9  E CK
      note: Lead your last club and trump it in dummy.
  10  N S3  E ST  S H4  W S7
      note: Lead a spade from dummy and trump it.
  11  S HT  W HK  N S4  E S8
      note: Lead a trump. West's ♥K takes it.
  12  W SA  N S6  E SJ  S HJ
      note: Trump West's ♠A.
  13  S HQ  W SQ  N S9  E SK
      note: Your last trump. 12 tricks: 4♥ made with two overtricks.

play recap:
  The plan: run your diamonds, then trump your black-suit losers.

  4♥ made with two overtricks. Partner had only 3 points, but your strong
  two-bid made sure she kept the auction open, and her raise was all you
  needed to bid game.
